# Prose documentation

Prose turns a source document into finished output in three steps. These guides
follow that path. If you are new to the library, read them in order.

1. **[The reader](reader.md)** explains the command language and shows how
   source text becomes ordinary Clojure data.
2. **[Evaluation](evaluation.md)** shows how Prose runs forms in order, handles
   namespace changes and included documents, and supports both Clojure and SCI.
3. **[Compilation](compilation.md)** turns the evaluated document into text,
   such as HTML, Markdown, or whatever you decide to program.
